<linker>
  <!--
    Feature switch TianWen.Lib.EmbeddedCatalogs. A consumer that never opens a catalog sets

        <RuntimeHostConfigurationOption Include="TianWen.Lib.EmbeddedCatalogs" Value="false" Trim="true" />

    and the trimmer / NativeAOT compiler drops every manifest resource named below from the output.
    The first consumer is tianwen-thumb.dll, the Explorer thumbnail provider: its code is 1.7 MB and
    these resources are 57 MB, so the switch is the difference between a 3 MB and a 60 MB shell DLL.

    Why the list lives HERE and not in the consumer: ILC indexes an embedded ILLink.Substitutions.xml
    by the module that embeds it, so a consumer's copy naming TianWen.Lib resources removes nothing
    (measured: 59.6 MB either way). Only this assembly's own file, or a global substitution file passed
    on the ILC command line, reaches them. (No double hyphen anywhere in this comment: XML forbids it,
    and the parser that enforces it is the test that pins this file.)

    The names are manifest resource names and must match the assembly exactly; there is no wildcard.
    EmbeddedCatalogFeatureSwitchTests pins this list against the built assembly, so adding a catalog
    without adding it here fails a test rather than silently shipping it in the thumbnail DLL. A
    resource that a THUMBNAIL genuinely needs would be the first one to leave this list.
  -->
  <assembly fullname="TianWen.Lib" feature="TianWen.Lib.EmbeddedCatalogs" featurevalue="false">
    <resource name="TianWen.Lib.Astrometry.Catalogs.Barnard.gs.gz" action="remove" />
    <resource name="TianWen.Lib.Astrometry.Catalogs.Barnard.shapes.json.lz" action="remove" />
